Z||000005||Songman||06-13-2001||03:08 AM||||I used to have a 350 Odyssey! Great fun machine! I'd take one over these 4-wheelers today anytime! Tipping don't bother me in a vehicle that I am strapped into with a roll cage around me. I rolled mine many times, got out and righted it and went on my way...<P>I wish I could find another one!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||RossT||06-13-2001||04:23 AM||||Bill, We recently baught a new minivan.  After much research, we narrowed it down to the Dodge GrandCaravan and the Honda. The Honda will hold its value more than the Dodge, but the Dodge has many more creature features that the Honda does not. PLEASE CHECK OUT <A HREF="http://www.edmunds.com" TARGET=_blank>www.edmunds.com</A>  and click "town hall" then "vans" and read everything you can.  Both of these vans have a history of trany problems (even though the Honda is new, they have had problems). My neighbor has the honda and the back hatch sheet metal can be dented with your thum!!  Other than that they love it.  I ended up with Dodge and am very happy. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||firstfiero||06-13-2001||09:08 AM||||  its Not only alot of fun but it's the safest atv you can buy. Roll cage and 4 point safety belt.Pretty f'ing fast to. definitly liked it more then my 3 wheeler.<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000008||Butter||06-13-2001||11:00 AM||||Bill,<BR>Used to work on the boogers when I was employeed by Vicker's Honda.  They started out as 250cc.  Only got to run them in the parking lot where we could check them out after repairs.  I liked the design of the drive system.  If memory serves they have a belt variable torque system that allows the engine to pull when it gets into its power band until it tops out.  Makes for great acceleration and fun.  Always wanted one but by the time I was able to afford it I was to damn big to fit in one, so I built a dune buggy instead.  I do occasionally see them when I've gone to Land Between the Lakes, Turkey Bay ATV area.  They still look like fun and I still have too much a$$ to enjoy one.  Oh well.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||11:56 AM||||Personally I think the safest All Terrain Vehicle (ATV?!) is a motorcross or enduro bike. You can get out of a lot more bad situations with 2 wheels than you can with 3 or 4, you can corner much faster if you need to, and you can always lay the bike down in a pinch.<P> Ive only ridden 3 wheelers and 4 wheelers a few times - no compairision to a motorcross bike - they look like motorized wheel chairs to me.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Butter||06-13-2001||12:13 PM||||Ken,<BR>I didn't know any ATV was safe and if you think they are then your not riding them right!  As far as bikes, trikes, and quads, there all a different ride with different ways of having fun.  Just don't peg your fun meter too much.||||reg||12
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||01:04 PM||||how does one measure too much, horizontal distance cleared or vertical height attain with wheels off the ground?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Butter||06-13-2001||03:38 PM||||Ken,<BR>By how many times you bounce and how far it is between the bounce skips when you come down.  HaHa. Caught too much air one time while riding my dirt bike and bounce landed in a blackberry thicket without even laying it down. Ouch!! Got in there with barely a scratch but gettin' out of there was a little bloody to say the least.  What a memory, but it was fun.||||reg||7
